Test assets for the dummy host, never shipped in the gem (test/ is dev-only).
Both MIT; the license banners ride inside the files.

Stimulus: the same UMD build poetry-core develops against, for the dommy
tier when poetry-core is an installed gem (no node_modules). Refresh with
`bundle exec rake vendor:stimulus` (copies the sibling's dist, records the
version here); `vendor:stimulus:verify` in the default chain fails on drift
side by side and skips against the released gem. The dist's own banner can
lag the package version (3.2.2 ships a "3.2.1" banner upstream).

Turbo: for the stable-id gate (real Turbo morphs under test). Update by
copying a newer dist and bumping the line above.
